{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And they enslaved.</b> He imposed many new cruelties upon them: first, to do his labor, and when he saw that their numbers did not diminish, he gave permission to the Egyptians and their officers to enslave them beyond the statutory limit of slaves — and this is בפרך. What Onkelos says and the expression פרוכין in piyyut is not correct at all. And when he saw that this did not help, then he called the midwives — who are officers over all the midwives — and commanded to kill every male born."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:46.663451039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}